# Typography

Tokens: `fontSize`, `fontWeight`, `lineHeight` in `web/lib/tokens.ts`.
Modular scale, 1.125 ratio.

## Scale

```
xs 12 | sm 14 | md 16 | lg 18 | xl 20 | 2xl 24 | 3xl 30 | 4xl 36 | 5xl 48
```

## Weights

```
regular 400 | medium 500 | semibold 600 | bold 700
```

## Rules

- Body text minimum `md` (16px). Never go below `sm` (14px) for readable text;
  `xs` is for metadata only.
- Headings use `semibold`; reserve `bold` for the single hero per view.
- Line height: `tight` for large headings, `snug` for UI labels, `normal` for
  body, `relaxed` for long-form docs.
- Numbers in dashboards: tabular-nums, right-aligned.
- One type family, weight does the hierarchy work. Do not mix families without
  intent.

## Accessibility

- Body contrast >= 4.5:1; large text >= 3:1 (see `17-accessibility`).
- Never use color alone to convey meaning; pair with text or icon.
